00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:06,850
Circle, circular line

2
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,440
Let's observe figure below:

3
00:00:16,590 --> 00:00:18,900
Circle

4
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:27,540
To draw circular line center O we do as follows:

5
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:43,210
Place pointed end of compass to create point O,

6
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:55,100
and take pencil end of compass to draw on paper one full round, we get a circular line with center O

7
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:08,190
connect center O with point A on circular line, we get radius OA of circle.

8
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:16,040
All radii of circle are equal.

9
00:01:18,490 --> 00:01:25,040
Connect points M, N on circular line through center O to form a straight segment

10
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:30,900
then MN is diameter of circle

11
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:41,520
In a circle, diameter length is 2 times radius.

12
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:53,530
Circumference, area of circle.

13
00:01:56,420 --> 00:02:00,560
Let C be circumference

14
00:02:01,390 --> 00:02:05,120
S be area of circle

15
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:08,640
d is diameter

16
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:14,460
r is radius of circle

17
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:26,440
To calculate circumference of circle we take diameter times 3.14

18
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:36,590
We have formula for calculating circumference of circle is:

19
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:56,910
C = d x 3.14 or C = r x 2 x 3.14

20
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:13,970
To calculate area of circle we take radius times radius times 3.14

21
00:03:17,930 --> 00:03:22,030
Formula for calculating area of circle is:

22
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:31,930
S = r x r x 3.14

